From 2f50e6c91847d49d73b6b97f28d77f0f9e2b94fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:21:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebrand to Clubs Ranked (blue/orange) and launch-readiness
 pass
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rebrand:
- New CR crest + wordmark (src/components/Logo.tsx), used in the navbar,
  footer, and homepage hero
- Blue/orange brand tokens in globals.css (was black/neon-green), CTA
  buttons (Sign up) now use the orange accent for contrast
- Restyled logged-out homepage hero with the new crest/colors
- Code-generated favicon, apple touch icon, and Open Graph/Twitter share
  image (src/app/icon.tsx, apple-icon.tsx, opengraph-image.tsx) replacing
  the old static favicon.ico
- Metadata: proper title template, openGraph/twitter tags, metadataBase
  pointing at clubsranked.co.uk

Security review (see SECURITY_REVIEW.md):
- The `squads`, `match_posts`, and `matches` UPDATE policies allowed any
  authenticated user to write ANY column (using(true)/check(true)) as an
  MVP trade-off for not having a service-role key. Verified every
  .update() call in src/app/api and added WITH CHECK column locks so only
  the columns app code actually writes stay open — everything else
  (squad name/captain/platform/region, post/match identity fields) is now
  locked to its existing value at the database layer.
  See supabase/migration_004_security_hardening.sql (apply to an existing
  project) — schema.sql is also updated so fresh installs get the
  hardened policies directly.
- Documented remaining accepted gap: squads.xp is still writable by any
  authenticated user pending a SECURITY DEFINER rewrite of XP awarding.

Legal basics:
- Added /privacy and /terms pages (UK GDPR-oriented, names Supabase/Vercel
  as processors, no third-party trackers)
- Added an EA trademark disclaimer to the footer
- Removed "coming soon" cash-matches language from the About page (was
  advertising a future feature pending unresolved UK gambling law
  review) in favor of a plain "no cash/wagering, none planned without
  legal review first" statement
- Added a "known limitations, for now" section to the About page
  (one-squad-per-user, no dispute-resolution flow) so this is
  communicated to users rather than left implicit

Support & cleanup:
- Added a support@clubsranked.co.uk contact link in the footer and About
  page
- Added supabase/cleanup_test_data.sql — a script to run once in the
  Supabase SQL editor to wipe test squads/matches before real users see
  the leaderboard (does not touch profiles/auth.users)

Verified: npx eslint . and npx next build both pass; spot-checked the
generated icon/OG images and the homepage/about/privacy pages in a
headless browser.
